<title>INDIA: India proposes cutting computer drive customs duty.</title>
<headline>India proposes cutting computer drive customs duty.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian government on Wednesday proposed reducing the customs duty on hard disk drives, floppy disk drives and CD-ROM drives to 10 percent from 20 percent.  </p>
<p>Finance Minister P. Chidambaram announced the proposed change in remarks to parliament during debate over the government's proposed Finance Bill for 1996/97 (April-March).</p>
<p>The proposed customs duty change would take effect upon parliamentary approval of the bill, expected by the end of the week.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
